WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.267 line:92%
-So I have to congratulate you.

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
300th episode of "Family Guy"
is coming up.

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:05.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. That is correct.
-That's incredible.

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:06.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:07.841 line:92%
Now that -- what is harder --

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:10.543
When you think back to yourself
as a child,

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:11.411 line:92%
what is harder to conceive,

00:00:11.411 --> 00:00:14.447
that you would do a cartoon that
would last 300 episodes

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:16.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
or that you would be nominated
for a Grammy

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:18.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the same category
as Bob Dylan,

00:00:18.952 --> 00:00:19.819 line:92%
'cause that happened for you?

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:23.490
-Yeah, you know, I wasn't even
sure I graduated high school.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:24.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I'm like --
-Yeah.

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:25.392 line:92%
-This is great. This is great.

00:00:25.392 --> 00:00:27.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Are you still not sure
if you graduated high school?

00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:29.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, we'll find --
I'll get back to you on that.

00:00:29.796 --> 00:00:33.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. But this is -- So, your
album, you sing standards.

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:34.100 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And you are --

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're nominated against
Bob Dylan,

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:37.604 size:84% position:42% line:92%
which is really trippy.

00:00:37.604 --> 00:00:38.138 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:39.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's -- just
slightly intimidating.

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:42.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And could be a problem.

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:42.542 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:44.511
Try not to get into a trash-talk
situation with him.

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:47.113
'Cause I feel you would not win.
-No, no, no.

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:47.947 line:92%
-So you -- This is standards.

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:50.550
How do you select the standards
that you're going to sing

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.117 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
on each album?

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:55.555
-You know, I try to find stuff
that isn't too heavily overdone.

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:59.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
I kind of dig through
old Broadway cast albums,

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:00.827 size:81% position:41% line:92%
through old songbooks.

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:04.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just try to find stuff
that is completely forgotten

00:01:04.297 --> 00:01:05.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
so you can kind of
make it new again.

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:07.300
-And what are you singing for us
tonight?

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:10.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is "Almost Like Being in
Love" from "Brigadoon."

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:11.438 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay, fantastic.

00:01:11.438 --> 00:01:13.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
So that's -- you also --
I just assume,

00:01:13.306 --> 00:01:14.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
and this is ignorance
on my part,

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:17.510 size:88% position:44%
that people who can sing
are so great at singing

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they don't need
to work on it.

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:22.115
But you actually went and
trained with the same group

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:23.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
of people
that trained Frank Sinatra.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:26.453
-They worked with Sinatra.
They worked with Streisand.

00:01:26.453 --> 00:01:31.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
They've actually trained a lot
of singers over the years.

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:33.259 line:92%
And they were both in their 90s

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:34.861 align:start size:94% position:6%
when I started working
with them.

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:36.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Are they --
Is it a family business?

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:38.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was a husband and wife.
-Okay.

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:40.366 line:92%
-That did this for decades.

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:41.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know, they both have
since passed away.

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:45.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
But they taught you
how to do it without help.

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:47.006 line:92%
-And what -- so when you --

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:49.943
So you go in to practicing
with these two 90-year-olds.

00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:53.279
Is there anything they told you
that you remembered?

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:54.147 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Like, that was helpful?

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:57.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They claimed
they were still having sex.

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:57.750 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I remember that.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:58.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really?
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:58.485 --> 00:02:01.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And they said, "Look, if you
are ever trying to find

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:04.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
the emotional place for your
songs, just remember that

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:07.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
there are 90-year-olds
who are still going at it."

00:02:07.427 --> 00:02:08.628 line:92%
-Exactly, exactly. No excuse.

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:10.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Is it true you're supposed to
show your teeth?

00:02:10.864 --> 00:02:13.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that something --
-That is correct, yeah, yeah.

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:15.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
Now, I had not known that.

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:16.769 line:92%
So explain what's behind that.

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:18.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, that's what
they always taught me.

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:20.440 line:92%
When you sing, show your teeth.

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:23.409
As crazy as that sounds
because it brightens the sound.

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:26.613
And all these tricks are things
if you're singing live

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:28.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
or if there is no
post-production help,

00:02:28.882 --> 00:02:30.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
You should be able
to sound good.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:33.887
And that's kind of -- that's
kind of the way they work.

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:35.455 line:92%
-Do you think they just, at 90,

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:37.891 align:start size:94% position:6%
had such an appreciation
for teeth?

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:38.424 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:40.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
They were like,
"If I have any regret,

00:02:40.527 --> 00:02:41.461 line:92%
I would have shown them more.

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:44.998
I wouldn't got them out there
more before it was too late."

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:46.666
So, I also want to congratulate
you,

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:48.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
season two of "Orville"
next year.

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:50.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
So that's really exciting
to get picked up.

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:51.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
Congratulations on that,
as well.

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:54.174 size:84% position:42%
-Thank you. Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:54.174 --> 00:02:55.675 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Thanks.

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:59.546
-How -- so obviously, you are --
you have the "Orville."

00:02:59.546 --> 00:03:02.782 size:78% position:39%
You did "Cosmos" with
Neil deGrasse Tyson.

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:04.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
You are a lover of space.
-Yes.

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:06.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I want to ask
this hypothetical,

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:07.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it seems we're getting
closer and closer

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:09.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
to people taking
recreational trips to space.

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:11.925 line:92%
Would you want to do that?

00:03:11.925 --> 00:03:13.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I would not.
-You don't.

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:16.329
-At least, I wouldn't want to be
among the first group.

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:16.729 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Gotcha.

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:18.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I would want to make sure
everything still works.

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:19.332 line:92%
Make sure everything is fine,

00:03:19.332 --> 00:03:22.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
everything's in order
and then maybe I'll go up.

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:22.635 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Uh-huh.

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:23.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'll be, like,
in the fifth or sixth.

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:25.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gotcha. Yeah.
I guess that's true.

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:27.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like the most expensive
tickets to space

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:28.408 line:92%
will be like five and six.

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:30.610
I think they'll have to discount
the first two trips.

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:32.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, you don't want to be
the guinea pig.

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:34.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. 'Cause I guess
the nice thing --

00:03:34.214 --> 00:03:37.984
because you, with your show,
it's a very controlled space

00:03:37.984 --> 00:03:40.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you are just doing it
on a sound stage.

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:41.254 line:92%
-Yeah, yeah, it's much better.

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:43.856
-How has it been trying to
create a serialized show

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:44.624 line:92%
that takes place in space?

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:47.493
Have you found it a different
challenge than "Family Guy"

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:48.161 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
in the writing?

00:03:48.161 --> 00:03:49.996 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-You know, it's nice

00:03:49.996 --> 00:03:53.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
because there's shockingly
little comedy.

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:53.666 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Uh-huh.

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:57.136
Whereas "Family Guy" you could
argue is more packed with jokes

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:58.638 line:92%
then anything on television.

00:03:58.638 --> 00:03:59.305 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:03.309
And it's kind of like I've been
doing comedy my whole career.

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:04.244 line:92%
And I'm a big sci-fi fan.

00:04:04.244 --> 00:04:07.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the thought of doing
something that is --

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:10.416
that's so far removed from that
was terrifying and thrilling

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:13.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
at the same time,
and, you know, I've loved it.

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:14.887 line:92%
I've loved every second of it.

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:15.455 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's great.

00:04:15.455 --> 00:04:17.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I want to ask
about Neil deGrasse Tyson.

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:21.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
There is an asteroid
that is named after you.

00:04:21.394 --> 00:04:22.061 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He tweeted this.

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:25.531 size:78% position:39%
I guess it's asteroid
70713 Seth MacFarlane

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:28.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
orbits the sun between
Mars and Jupiter.

00:04:28.468 --> 00:04:29.535 line:92%
No chance of hitting Earth.

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:31.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That is my given name,
is 70713.

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:32.105 line:92%
-So how did that come about?

00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:34.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do you get an asteroid
named after yourself?

00:04:34.374 --> 00:04:37.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, I think it was
because of "Cosmos."

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:37.744 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, okay. Gotcha.

00:04:37.744 --> 00:04:40.380
-I think he kind of pulled
a couple of his strings --

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:41.114 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-So that's basically --

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:43.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
if you want to get
an asteroid named after you,

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:45.852
cozy up to Neil deGrasse Tyson.
-Apparently so.

00:04:45.852 --> 00:04:46.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Apparently so.

00:04:46.853 --> 00:04:48.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I knew he knew
a lot of that stuff.

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:50.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn't think they called him
up and were like,

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:52.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hey, man.
We're looking for a name."

00:04:52.659 --> 00:04:54.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I guess...
-The politics of asteroids

00:04:54.761 --> 00:04:57.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
is something that I'm --
I can't help you.

00:04:57.063 --> 00:04:57.997 line:92%
-And I've got to be honest.

00:04:57.997 --> 00:04:59.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't think
I'm ever going to learn.

00:04:59.399 --> 00:05:02.235
I' just gonna -- I'm just gonna
let that take its course.

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:04.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It almost never comes up
at parties.

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:05.238 line:92%
-So, it came up this week,

00:05:05.238 --> 00:05:07.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I want to get your take
on this, as well,

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:10.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you're now living in
this world of sci-fi,

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:13.313
that in 2007, the Pentagon
basically put aside some --

00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:16.115
I don't know if it's called
dark money or black money,

00:05:16.115 --> 00:05:19.786
where they basically have been
checking out UFOs since 2007.

00:05:19.786 --> 00:05:22.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, this is money
in the budget.

00:05:22.555 --> 00:05:26.426 size:81% position:41%
Do you think that --
that UFOs maybe exist?

00:05:26.426 --> 00:05:30.530
-From what I have read
and what -- in talking to Neil,

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:33.466
that what they were looking for
was not necessarily --

00:05:33.466 --> 00:05:36.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
nobody gives a [bleep]
about aliens there.

00:05:36.402 --> 00:05:36.836 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:39.238
-They're looking for things that
might possibly be, you know,

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:41.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
bits of -- provide bits of
intelligence

00:05:41.574 --> 00:05:42.508 line:92%
from other countries, I guess.

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:45.778
I don't -- I think the UFO
enthusiasts sort of got ahold

00:05:45.778 --> 00:05:49.115
of that and said,
"Oh, they're looking for UFOs."

00:05:49.115 --> 00:05:49.782 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-But I think it's --

00:05:49.782 --> 00:05:52.251
I think it's highly likely there
is alien life.

00:05:52.251 --> 00:05:55.555
I think it's highly unlikely
that we have been visited.

00:05:55.555 --> 00:05:55.955 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Uh-huh.

00:05:55.955 --> 00:06:01.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think if we spent more time
listening for signals,

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:02.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
and less time, you know,
looking for evidence

00:06:02.795 --> 00:06:05.365
that they had come here, I think
we're probably better served.

00:06:05.365 --> 00:06:08.534
-Interesting. So you're saying
put the money into just like --

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:10.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Like, surveillance.

00:06:10.103 --> 00:06:10.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:12.438 size:84% position:42%
-Listen to outer space.
-Listen to outer space.

00:06:12.438 --> 00:06:16.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, send out some, like --
you know, bugs.

00:06:16.476 --> 00:06:17.777 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Or that, yeah.

00:06:17.777 --> 00:06:20.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Look, I feel like they've got
to give us this money

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:20.780 line:92%
and we can figure this out

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:21.981 size:88% position:44%
because I would love to
get to the bottom of it.

00:06:21.981 --> 00:06:23.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much for sticking
around and singing a song.

00:06:23.716 --> 00:06:25.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
-My pleasure. Always.
-Always a pleasure to see you.

00:06:25.918 --> 00:06:27.754 line:92%
Seth MacFarlane, everybody.

